 "notes": "Headline result: 95% C.L. limit on the axion-gluon coupling C_G/f_a from a search for an oscillating neutron EDM (Fig. 4 top). Curve is the envelope (minimum) of the thick red (long time-base, ILL 1998-2002) and thick blue (short time-base, PSI 2015-2016) curves, extracted from the vector PDF psi_ill_axion_limits_v7.pdf in the e-print; axis calibration verified against the quoted peak sensitivity f_a/C_G ~ 1e21 GeV for m_a < 1e-23 eV. Converted to the canonical oscillating-EDM coupling via Eq. (2): d_n = 2.4e-16 (C_G/f_a) a_0 cos(m_a t) e.cm, i.e. g_d = 2.4e-16 e.cm x (C_G/f_a) with 1 e.cm = 1.5346e13 GeV^-1 (Heaviside-Lorentz, e = sqrt(4 pi alpha)), so g_d [GeV^-2] = 3.683e-3 x (C_G/f_a) [GeV^-1]. Paper assumes axions saturate rho_DM_local ~ 0.4 GeV/cm^3; limit scales as sqrt(rho_a). The high-mass end (1.6e-17 eV, ~3 mHz, the PSI cycle rate) is where the blue curve rises vertically out of the plot; last point is the curve value just before that rise. The paper also sets an axion-wind limit on the axion-nucleon coupling C_N/f_a (Fig. 4 bottom), not reported here since the oscillating-EDM/gluon limit is presented as the main result.",
